\pard\b\fs20 Cerberus Fossae\b0\par
\fs16\par
Shaped by former volcanic activity, this hilly area formed over long spans of time. \par
The latest analyses reject the theory that there is a cryosphere here; instead, some deposits of fossil fuels have been found.\par
At the time of landing, a dusty sandstorm is raging over the area, but that shouldn't be a problem.\par
